# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

~> **Note:** This resource is behind a feature flag. Set the environment variable `YBM_FF_AMP=true` to use it.

Set `environment_id` for a cluster in a BYOC environment; leave it unset for a shared cluster.

`cpu`, `memory`, `allowed_cidrs` and `pg_settings` can be changed in place. Changing `cluster_name`, `branch_name`, `endpoint_name`, `role`, `connectivity_mode` or `environment_id` replaces the endpoint. A `read_write` endpoint requires `password`, which cannot be changed after creation; a `read_only` endpoint takes none. A branch has at most one `read_write` endpoint, and the cluster resources already create one, named `primary`, on `main`.

